This matters because the test doesn't actually exercise the property "allow rule cannot override a guard" via a path where the allow-rule check is evaluated and then rejected — it short-circuits before that. A reader may incorrectly believe the test proves the allow-rule is checked and fails, when in fact it is never checked.

