The existing comment on the allow-rules block says "A global per-tool/per-command pre-approval that skips the policy." This is accurate but does not surface the non-obvious consequence: a matched allow rule also skips Plan's read-only restriction (and AcceptEdits, and DontAsk — but DontAsk is already called out). Since this is per design, a one-line addition eliminates any future "is this a bug?" comment thread:

```rust
